#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:5
#: 6bb68b2ba98c440ab373e3839dd6127f
msgid "High Quality Bixler 1.1 Build (APM2.x)"
msgstr "高质量 Bixler 1.1 组装（APM2.x）"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:7
#: 91015d27e603472d9fb6cbf72d521023
msgid "This article describes a well planned Bixler Build (by Dave Smith)."
msgstr "本文介绍了一次精心规划的 Bixler 组装过程（作者：Dave Smith）。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:13
#: 6522e3b5cff542938eef71c889b1101e
msgid "Overview"
msgstr "概述"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:15
#: 4dde68c4acc243759d4581a37c6a7ca7
msgid ""
"I have seen some really horrific pictures on the internet of Bixlers with "
"everything taped to the outside. After digging through the internet, I found"
" the answers I needed to build my plane, but the learning curve was pretty "
"steep."
msgstr ""
"我在互联网上看到过一些非常糟糕的 Bixler 照片，所有东西都用胶带粘在机身外面。经过大量搜索，我找到了组装所需的答案，但学习曲线相当陡峭。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:20
#: 50406f514db54865bea00ed61c1ff6f7
msgid ""
"**Hopefully I can help somebody out and save them a lot of frustration by "
"logging my whole build.**"
msgstr "**希望通过记录我的完整组装过程，能够帮助大家节省大量的挫折感。**"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:24
#: b051ad4183d5422c85bef14e4fefbafd
msgid "The Equipment List"
msgstr "设备清单"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:26
#: 3b03453a753a4af08c5e78365a2ecdb5
msgid ""
"`Bixler 1.1 ARF <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/h-king-bixler-1-1-epo-1400mm-"
"glider-arf.html>`__ (HobbyKing)"
msgstr ""
"`Bixler 1.1 ARF <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/h-king-bixler-1-1-epo-1400mm-"
"glider-arf.html>`__ （HobbyKing）"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:28
#: d0b6084d64e44dfea98fc008d034a074
msgid ""
"`Motor <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/turnigy-multistar-2216-800kv-14pole-"
"multi-rotor-outrunner-v2.html>`_ (HobbyKing) or other 2216 size 800-1000KV "
"motor"
msgstr ""
"`电机 <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/turnigy-multistar-2216-800kv-14pole-multi-"
"rotor-outrunner-v2.html>`_ （HobbyKing）或其他 2216 规格 800-1000KV 电机"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:30
#: 3cd8f20fc10f449e974d024cddfbc104
msgid ""
"`ESC <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/turnigy-basic-18a-v3-1-speed-"
"controller.html>`__ (HobbyKing) or other 18-20A ESC"
msgstr ""
"`ESC <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/turnigy-basic-18a-v3-1-speed-"
"controller.html>`__ （HobbyKing）或其他 18-20A ESC"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:32
#: ae8f0f7e44a241909f6e2b7715acec16
msgid ""
"`SBEC <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/turnigy-5a-8-26v-sbec-for-lipo.html>`__ "
"(HobbyKing) - (Optional) 5A BEC"
msgstr ""
"`SBEC <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/turnigy-5a-8-26v-sbec-for-lipo.html>`__ "
"（HobbyKing）——（可选）5A BEC"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:34
#: 2a98df8b518440dcb7329c8bdd1e0e3d
msgid ""
"`Motor mount <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/hobbyking-bixler-and-"
"bixler-2-motor-mount-upgrade.html>`__   (HobbyKing) - (for spinning bigger "
"props)"
msgstr ""
"`电机座 <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/hobbyking-bixler-and-bixler-2-motor-mount-"
"upgrade.html>`__ （HobbyKing）——（用于驱动更大螺旋桨）"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:35
#: caa09f4dc0f94d5e87eb4595ec3df4ae
msgid "APM 2.6 with separate GPS/compass. (see note below)"
msgstr "APM 2.6，配独立 GPS/罗盘。（见下方说明）"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:36
#: ced511e24f9249428fda6bb7f555af00
msgid "Radio: Spektrum DX8 and RX or any other 5 channel or higher system."
msgstr "遥控器：Spektrum DX8 及接收机，或其他任何 5 通道及以上系统。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:37
#: a5a4dde20d684b0281271b6e020a406c
msgid ""
"Prop: APC 8x4E . Pusher or puller may be used since motor direction is "
"easily changed just by swapping wires."
msgstr "螺旋桨：APC 8x4E。可使用推进式或拉进式，因为只需交换导线即可轻松更改电机方向。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:38
#: 1de5df3e08f74bd4a9a963d878ac0724
msgid ""
"Y-servo-cable to connect both aileron servos together to one autopilot "
"output."
msgstr "Y 形舵机线缆，用于将两个副翼舵机连接至飞控的同一输出通道。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:41
#: b101fab205f349eb95e266251fee65da
msgid ""
"This autopilot is no longer supported. See the current autopilot "
":ref:`list<common-autopilots>`. OmnibusF4 Pro V3 is an inexpensive "
"alternative. Any UBLOX MN-8 class GPS works well, such as a BN-220. A "
"compass (gps/compass combo parts are available) is not necessary for "
"ArduPilot on planes."
msgstr ""
"此飞控已不再受支持。请参阅当前飞控 :ref:`列表<common-autopilots>`。OmnibusF4 Pro V3 是一款低价替代方案。任何"
" UBLOX MN-8 级别的 GPS 均可良好运行，例如 BN-220。对于固定翼飞机，ArduPilot "
"不强制要求罗盘（GPS/罗盘组合模块已有售）。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:44
#: b51e3f5b47184b97ad01bcd32c432e2b
msgid "Getting Started"
msgstr "入门"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:46
#: 8d19793484704850b3ca72371edce56a
msgid ""
"About using an external SBEC: I chose to do this because I am an RC heli "
"guy, and I often use servos that draw ridiculous current."
msgstr "关于使用外置 SBEC：我选择这样做，因为我是一名遥控直升机玩家，经常使用电流消耗极大的舵机。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:48
#: e4d6f52a5f444ad9bccfc0914409ad22
msgid ""
"If you power the servos separately from the BEC built into the ESC, there is"
" less chance of either one shutting down due to over-current draw."
msgstr "如果将舵机的供电与 ESC 内置 BEC 分开，发生任一因过电流关断的概率就会降低。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:50
#: 8cd0d70987fb43b9840378a6b320b13e
msgid "But you also add a second electronic device that can fail."
msgstr "但这样也增加了第二个可能故障的电子器件。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:51
#: 1d37089cf1ca4f46bed252e73362d48d
msgid ""
"When the motor is at max throttle and servos are fully deflected, such as on"
" a windy day, the separate BEC gives you some headroom."
msgstr "在大风天气，电机全油门且舵机完全偏转时，独立 BEC 可以提供一定的余量。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:53
#: 0636c8c1da2f4f9ab735a5479fc4a3a8
msgid ""
"There are smaller, inexpensive BECs on the market that use up less space "
"than what I have pictured."
msgstr "市面上有更小、更实惠的 BEC，占用空间比我图示中的小。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:55
#: 8f9b04593c9545c1bcb4c1654029446c
msgid ""
"This is totally optional. The ESC's BEC will work well and reliably in this "
"application."
msgstr "这完全是可选的。在本应用中，ESC 内置的 BEC 可以稳定可靠地工作。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:58
#: e3c5f400ec0f47a7b7d2eeca4b6dbb9f
msgid "Programming the ESC"
msgstr "ESC 编程"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:60
#: e2b4c56448434ea1bee9214653db09c2
msgid ""
"Using the ESC's setup instructions, set the ESC's low voltage cutoff to its "
"lowest setting to allow   the autopilot battery level failsafe feature do "
"its job. (be sure to enable it!)"
msgstr "按照 ESC 的设置说明，将 ESC 的低压截止设置为最低值，以便飞控的电池低压失控保护功能正常工作。（务必启用该功能！）"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:61
#: d655dc0e08fe48eb943f49f5cc57db24
msgid ""
"Don't worry about motor direction; you can just switch two of the motor "
"wires if the motor spins backwards."
msgstr "无需担心电机方向；如果电机反转，只需交换两根电机导线即可。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:63
#: 8d4766ae8a10488597cd7e45501a3a0f
msgid ""
"Follow the :ref:`ESC setup guide <common-esc-calibration>` to calibrate the "
"ESC"
msgstr "按照 :ref:`ESC 校准指南 <common-esc-calibration>` 对 ESC 进行校准"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:66
#: 72d392fa126342a6abd14a5fd612fdb5
msgid "Wiring the ESC and BEC"
msgstr "ESC 与 BEC 接线"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:68
#: c0760daa79ff47fda1964b7344f19ebe
msgid ""
"I chose to use EC3 connectors in my build, because all of my batteries have "
"them. XT-60 are just fine."
msgstr "我在组装中选用了 EC3 连接器，因为我所有的电池都使用该接口。XT-60 同样完全可以。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:71
#: c1c87aad7781423d9eed2fb994054e0d
msgid "If you do not use an external SBEC, skip to the last step."
msgstr "如果不使用外置 SBEC，请跳至最后一步。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:73
#: 85f4874d336b4ac08d7747a359b9326d
msgid "Cut the center servo power lead off of the ESC's BEC at the connector."
msgstr "在连接器处剪断 ESC BEC 的中间舵机电源引线。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:74
#: a53623805cc64700a6af20fceb397251
msgid ""
"Solder the SBEC power cables along with the ESC power cables into your "
"connector (this can be a little tricky). #. Get the solder hot in a "
"connector and insert an ESC wire. #. Keep the connection hot and slip the "
"BEC power wire in next to it."
msgstr ""
"将 SBEC 电源线与 ESC 电源线一起焊入连接器（这可能有点棘手）。#. 在连接器中将焊锡加热，插入 ESC 导线。#. 保持连接处高温，将 BEC"
" 电源线紧靠其旁插入。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:78
#: fce207bad05e4d64b93a9c6cd055c397
msgid ""
"I chose to run my servos at 5V  from the SBEC. #. There is a jumper on the "
"end of it that lets you select 5 or 6 V. #. Before you reinstall the "
"electronics secure the jumper on the SBEC with a glob of hot glue or shoe "
"goo."
msgstr ""
"我选择通过 SBEC 以 5V 为舵机供电。#. SBEC 末端有一个跳线，可选择 5V 或 6V。#. 重新安装电子设备前，用热熔胶或鞋胶将 SBEC"
" 上的跳线固定好。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:81
#: 6c263ca4c6d744dfa83cbd24217ecbf2
msgid ""
"Pull the center (red) pin and wire from the ESC receiver connector. #. This "
"disconnects the built in BEC from the ESC. You don't need it since it since "
"we are using a separate (dedicated) BEC. #. Tuck the ESCs BEC wire away with"
" heat shrink tubing over the end. #. You will need access to it if you need "
"to re-program the ESC."
msgstr ""
"从 ESC 接收机连接器中拔出中间（红色）引脚和导线。#. 这将断开 ESC 内置 BEC 的连接，由于我们使用了独立的专用 BEC，它已无需再用。#."
" 用热缩管套住 ESC BEC 线的端头并收纳好。#. 若日后需重新编程 ESC，仍需使用它。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:85
#: 53a514035c074e0e9bbfc777c3d9f183
msgid ""
"Add 100mm 14 gauge motor lead extensions with 3.5mm banana plugs to make it "
"easier to wire the Bixler's motor later."
msgstr "在电机引线上添加 100mm 14 号规格延长线并配 3.5mm 香蕉插头，以便后续为 Bixler 的电机接线。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:87
#: c882b268cdbd4795bab2c4f351c02377
msgid "**Here it is ready to go:**"
msgstr "**成品准备就绪：**"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:93
#: 5f24468c6e794212b2802071fc0aa062
msgid "Setting up the Autopilot, Sensors, and Optional Equipment"
msgstr "设置飞控、传感器及可选设备"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:95
#: b6ee6e516c5d4e499ee8c4f43533ce2c
msgid ""
"The purpose of this article is to detail the aircraft build, not the APM. "
"There are many documents in the wiki covering the APM, sensors, and tuning. "
"`Airplane walk-through <https://ardupilot.org/plane/docs/arduplane-"
"setup.html>`_ ."
msgstr ""
"本文的目的是详细介绍飞机的组装，而非 APM 本身。Wiki 中有大量文档涵盖 APM、传感器和调参。`固定翼操作指南 "
"<https://ardupilot.org/plane/docs/arduplane-setup.html>`_ 。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:100
#: 60762001db824cf2be56cf5eb9909eb1
msgid "Mount the autopilot and install the wiring"
msgstr "安装飞控并布线"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:102
#: b86dffd24a7646b3a1a3f693ae0ed927
msgid ""
"Make a 45 x 100 mm mounting plate for the autopilot using 5mm plywood (or "
"plastic or fiberglass board)."
msgstr "用 5mm 夹板（或塑料板、玻璃纤维板）制作一块 45 x 100 mm 的飞控安装底板。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:104
#: 4dd469f7c5e04a38a4518c5cb5d91248
msgid ""
"Use a 1\" square of Kyosho Zeal Gel or Dubro foam under each corner of the "
"autopilot to provide vibration suppression."
msgstr "在飞控四个角下方各垫一块 1 英寸见方的 Kyosho Zeal Gel 或 Dubro 泡沫，以提供减震支撑。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:106
#: fc1b011cb49c486e95e1d42832999eb2
msgid ""
"Zeal has high strength double sided adhesive, but if your pads do not, "
"consider using \"Welders Glue\" available at Amazon or Lowes."
msgstr "Zeal 自带高强度双面胶，如果您的减震垫没有，可考虑使用「焊工胶」，亚马逊或 Lowes 均有售。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:108
#: 96e2ce70225c4f73a6e66c473ae9d1e2
msgid ""
"Re Welder's Glue: it is contact cement. Lightly cover each surface you wish "
"to bond and let them dry for about five minutes."
msgstr "关于「焊工胶」：这是一种接触胶。在要粘合的两个表面各涂薄薄一层，晾干约五分钟。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:110
#: 9e92dda11bf444c7a685d6a2a5558981
msgid ""
"Then carefully align and put the two surfaces together and for immediate "
"bonding."
msgstr "然后仔细对准并将两个表面压合，即可立即粘牢。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:112
#: e61f958f4c234749baebd6d065b3daf1
msgid ""
"I will also use Welder's Glue for assembling the foam air frame and building"
" an access door in the fuselage."
msgstr "我还会用「焊工胶」粘接泡沫机身并在机身上制作检修舱门。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:115
#: 4b2d4a368a3143e9b0eb6dd9735bd295
msgid ""
"**The APM autopilot mounted on the plate: (Pictured are the stock cables to "
"the GPS. I actually used longer 30cm cables)**"
msgstr "**安装在底板上的 APM 飞控：（图中为连接 GPS 的原装线缆，实际我换用了 30cm 的较长线缆）**"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:122
#: 23e38ea41382459cb1052d3552959608
msgid "Preparing the Fuselage"
msgstr "机身准备"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:124
#: 18670fdafa614752be2532da37274f5e
msgid ""
"For this build, the APM is mounted inverted and we want to get it level with"
" the fuselage (level with the line of flight)."
msgstr "在本次组装中，APM 倒置安装，我们需要让它与机身水平（与飞行方向水平）。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:126
#: a00a1ad668c74edfb3971a47fc5fdee9
msgid ""
"You can see that the wing has a positive angle of attack when the APM is "
"level."
msgstr "可以看到，当 APM 保持水平时，机翼具有正迎角。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:128
#: 8b7e4a0e4bd74af7bf3ce70107df74e6
msgid ""
"If you just stick the APM to the bottom or top of the fuselage it will not "
"be level, but this will be compensated for if you set the \"LEVEL\" position"
" to be such that the wing has a few degrees of angle of attack when doing "
"the :ref:`Accelerometer calibration <common-accelerometer-calibration>`."
msgstr ""
"如果直接将 APM 粘在机身底部或顶部，它将不会保持水平，但如果在 :ref:`加速度计校准 <common-accelerometer-"
"calibration>` 时将「水平」位置设置为机翼有数度迎角时的状态，这一偏差会得到补偿。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:130
#: 218170c4e15a4ba386888caa6c0880ce
msgid ""
"I removed some of the foam below the top inside of the fuselage to get the "
"APM level:"
msgstr "我去除了机身内顶部的部分泡沫，以使 APM 保持水平："

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:137
#: fec4de3e2370417fb939adc10f7067d6
msgid "Component Placement"
msgstr "零件布局"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:139
#: 1a5a27e5c11641039d4b722aee7e6f00
msgid "Here is the APM set in place with some of the components."
msgstr "这是 APM 和部分零件就位后的效果。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:140
#: 40413d92b5f945b2a449fb378c8b7245
msgid "At this point you should mark where your access panel will be."
msgstr "此时应标记出检修面板的位置。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:146
#: fb1198186a0643dca23ffec983d48652
msgid "Trimming the Fuselage"
msgstr "机身修剪"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:148
#: 7cb6b10e77e04f04bbe914c2b8f9cf53
msgid "I originally cut too much and the fuselage was really weak."
msgstr "我最初切得过多，导致机身非常脆弱。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:149
#: 1df5e667a6c6439d9a27f92a81019a7a
msgid "No problem; with some hot glue you can easily fix any boo-boos."
msgstr "没关系，用热熔胶可以轻松修复任何失误。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:150
#: a87beb05672842f7a2111ff15a29ed6f
msgid ""
"In the picture below you want to cut the lower portion and leave the area I "
"have labeled \"Do Not Cut\"."
msgstr "在下图中，您需要切除下方部分，保留标注「请勿切割」的区域。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:152
#: 060799734687410f9d3aad91505ce2d3
msgid ""
"You will have ample room to access the APM Inputs and Outputs, as well as "
"the USB port and other pins."
msgstr "这样您将有足够空间接触 APM 的输入输出端口、USB 接口及其他引脚。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:154
#: 7d6148bcc28747b4b4183b19f1f4f939
msgid "Cut straight through the foam so that the panel will open easily."
msgstr "将泡沫切割平直，使面板能够轻松开合。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:159
#: d49b1350e34b4a648688761729a2a3a2
msgid "Now match up the two halves to mark the cuts for the right side."
msgstr "现在将两半机身对齐，标记右侧的切割位置。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:160
#: db1bdf2f0a5245c2809b7bdaf83d347c
msgid ""
"Cut a larger access panel out of the other (right) half of the fuselage so "
"you can access the USB port on the APM."
msgstr "在机身另一（右）半侧切出更大的检修面板，以便接触 APM 上的 USB 接口。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:166
#: ecc9a7d7a65c425495ad9557fce80940
msgid "Cut a bevel along the long axis of the large panel we already cut out."
msgstr "沿已切出大面板的长轴方向切割斜面。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:168
#: 69bd52d1b4a04849b86ea293bb24e629
msgid ""
"I think that my picture is incorrect below; make this cut on the panel from "
"the \\ **right half of the fuselage**."
msgstr "我认为下图所示有误；请在 **机身右半部分** 的面板上进行此切割。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:170
#: 13810540551b4ec6aa7d0979354d34e2
msgid ""
"This is not the edge where the two halves of the fuselage join, but the cut "
"near the wing."
msgstr "这不是两半机身拼合处的边缘，而是靠近机翼的切割处。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:176
#: 37910e23255541df8af63c77009837c6
msgid ""
"Now, make a Welder's glue hinge where the bevel (that we just cut) meets the"
" fuselage."
msgstr "现在，在斜面（刚切好的）与机身相接处制作一个「焊工胶铰链」。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:178
#: 25d2fa67bc5744649890723caa8076bb
msgid "This creates a hinge for the panel that is invisible and super cool."
msgstr "这样制作出的铰链既隐形又非常酷。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:179
#: aa0002a2c2004afcb1d7b89cde299c0f
msgid ""
"Don't worry, custom foamies use this type of hinge for hundreds of flights."
msgstr "放心，定制泡沫机型使用此类铰链可以飞行数百次。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:181
#: 215ed4d0d8264e9a87b61fbca4bd3053
msgid ""
"Here is a `link <http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S-8PGFJqqMM>`_ to a YouTube "
"video explaining how to make a Welder's hinge:"
msgstr ""
"这里有一个 `链接 <http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S-8PGFJqqMM>`_，介绍如何制作「焊工胶铰链」的 "
"YouTube 视频："

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:182
#: ee2d4cf8092c433893dcb80a5d3890ab
msgid "The panel should look like this when the Welder's hinge is complete:"
msgstr "「焊工胶铰链」完成后，面板应如下图所示："

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:188
#: bef45d8e67794fae874ccf198df119de
msgid "Assemble the Fuselage"
msgstr "组装机身"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:190
#: 117ca55fb2084802823f0c8509d883e3
msgid "So now I am going to fast forward a little bit."
msgstr "现在我将稍微快进一下。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:191
#: b2788190b4914ef5b4ef79a6baea61d9
msgid ""
"Follow the Bixler instructions and glue the halves of the fuselage together."
msgstr "按照 Bixler 说明书，将机身两半粘合在一起。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:193
#: e45a3ace3eed45d0899b904076880420
msgid ""
"Again, I use Welder's glue, applying a thin bead to each half, letting them "
"get tacky, and then assembling the halves."
msgstr "同样，我使用「焊工胶」，在每半侧涂抹细细一条，待其变黏后再将两半拼合。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:195
#: e6cf61dc084640e49520026a2a0a0322
msgid ""
"Run the motor cables from the ESC to the motor before you assemble the two "
"halves."
msgstr "在组装两半机身之前，先将电机电缆从 ESC 穿到电机处。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:197
#: 2add119b4576429685a5be7b09fa3df9
msgid ""
"No worries if you don't, but it will save you the trouble of trying to "
"attach the motor leads with needle nose pliers and hemostats."
msgstr "如果忘记，也不用担心，只是需要用尖嘴钳和止血钳费些力气连接电机引线。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:199
#: 8de50e2e5a3c4a419cfc79b55e1edd2d
msgid ""
"You should also check the rotation of the motor so that you do not have to "
"switch motor leads for a motor spinning in reverse."
msgstr "还应检查电机转向，避免组装后才发现电机反转而需要更换电机引线。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:203
#: 93a024058a664360a895873a25df78b5
msgid "COMPONENT Installation Details"
msgstr "零件安装细节"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:205
#: 87f3650a30fb41f987d5ffc21f4ac122
msgid ""
"Below I have the fuselage glued together and the components glued in place."
msgstr "以下是机身粘合完毕、各零件粘好就位的效果。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:207
#: b0873bd627a941719d718228ed630865
msgid "I like hot glue for this detail."
msgstr "我喜欢用热熔胶处理这些细节。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:208
#: fe0384f938b4483790a19a5a833b0602
msgid ""
"Notice that I glued a 3mm carbon fiber rod across the access hatch for added"
" rigidity."
msgstr "注意，我在检修舱口横向粘了一根 3mm 碳纤维杆以增强刚性。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:214
#: 77b9cabf8ffd4cdfac09cbd544067ca8
msgid ""
"At this point, space is becoming a concern. Using a smaller BEC will help "
"you out."
msgstr "此时，空间开始变得紧张。使用更小的 BEC 会有所帮助。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:216
#: 78c40f03004047d3a1567f9623fe499a
msgid ""
"You will notice that we have put nothing in the nose so far, and all of our "
"components are pretty tightly tucked under the wing."
msgstr "您会注意到到目前为止机头部分什么都没放，所有零件都紧凑地塞在机翼下方。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:218
#: 9948a77249d048ed9aa57a2f9ba03577
msgid "I did this so that we can utilize bigger batteries in future builds."
msgstr "这样做是为了在将来的组装中可以使用更大的电池。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:219
#: a8fd50101ab64d25ad4e7aeabe6a1045
msgid ""
"This time around I am using an airspeed sensor which is recommended, but not"
" necessary if you are on a first-time build budget."
msgstr "这次我使用了空速传感器，推荐使用，但如果是初次组装预算有限，也不是必须的。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:221
#: 866a890ce0d547d48e5d41872012b53a
msgid ""
"To make space for batteries, I mounted the airspeed sensor board and "
"receiver to the bottom of the canopy hatch:"
msgstr "为给电池腾出空间，我将空速传感器电路板和接收机安装在舱盖内侧："

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:228
#: a83cbf31c37c4d6eadb5c1c33dc72052
msgid "Complete The Construction"
msgstr "完成组装"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:230
#: d3f983449beb4580a567ffbc605a7645
msgid ""
"Use a Y servo splitter cable for the ailerons, although using separate "
"autopilot outputs would allow the use of :ref:`flaperons<flaperons-on-"
"plane>`."
msgstr "副翼使用 Y 形舵机分线线缆，不过使用独立的飞控输出可支持 :ref:`副翼兼扰流板<flaperons-on-plane>` 功能。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:231
#: de5717fe066f4878a33b185757374d52
msgid ""
"I am quite happy with this setup because you can get the CG perfect with "
"Zippy 3s 2200mAh Lipo batteries. I was able to use up to 3000 mAh batts."
msgstr "我对这套方案非常满意，使用 Zippy 3s 2200mAh 锂电池可以完美平衡重心。我最大使用了 3000mAh 的电池。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:233
#: 5c9df19cb4ed4ce59a84a58c8a4c057a
msgid ""
"I mounted the GPS/Compass on the right wing after removing just a small "
"amount of material."
msgstr "我在右侧机翼上去除少量材料后安装了 GPS/罗盘。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:235
#: 53b3588e6df34f35869faa1f90534b52
msgid ""
"Having it sitting up high on the wing is not ideal, but I wanted to get it "
"away from the fuselage and all of the current-carrying electronics. I "
"ultimately ran the cables under the wing along the carbon fiber rod, which "
"is much smoother. If you do not use a compass, the gps can be mounted "
"anywhere as long as its upper surface (antenna) faces the sky."
msgstr ""
"让它高高地架在机翼上并不理想，但我希望让它远离机身及所有载流电子设备。最终我将线缆沿碳纤维杆穿在机翼下方，这样更整洁。如果不使用罗盘，GPS "
"可以安装在任何地方，只要其上表面（天线面）朝向天空即可。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:242
#: 7531543dfc7c49a8b1cf5ca69d83f4ff
msgid "Tuning and Flight Performance"
msgstr "调参与飞行性能"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:244
#: 8fe9b7427c2a49f8923300c44beea739
msgid ""
"To get the best motor and propeller for my build, I used `eCalc "
"<http://ecalc.ch>`__ , which is worth the money. You can also use "
":ref:`Drive Calculator<drivecalculator-guide>`, which is free."
msgstr ""
"为了给我的组装选择最佳电机和螺旋桨，我使用了 `eCalc <http://ecalc.ch>`__，物有所值。您也可以使用免费的 "
":ref:`Drive Calculator<drivecalculator-guide>`。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:247
#: 0170dd4f320f4bd3a0a6e096896fd8cc
msgid ""
"After going through the wizard in Mission Planner, you should have a compass"
" that points correctly, and a properly working GPS. I found that the initial"
" settings were quite flyable, and using the Autotune to give very good "
"results."
msgstr ""
"在 Mission Planner 完成向导后，您应该拥有一个指向正确的罗盘和正常工作的 GPS。我发现初始设置相当可飞，使用 Autotune "
"可以获得非常好的效果。"

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:251
#: ef49e728d3464d048949636d3d97959c
msgid ""
"At 6 m/s the aircraft becomes unstable and begins to tip stall, so keep your"
" cruise speed higher than this. Using a 2216-800 kV motor and and 8-4.7 prop"
" configuration and a 3000 mAh battery, I was able to achieve **80 minute "
"flights** at 12 m/s air speed!"
msgstr ""
"在 6m/s 以下飞机会变得不稳定并开始翼尖失速，因此请保持巡航空速高于此值。使用 2216-800kV 电机、8-4.7 螺旋桨配置以及 "
"3000mAh 电池，我实现了 12m/s 空速下 **80 分钟的飞行时间**！"
